216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E ( The programme aims to familiarise participants with emerging AI technologies and their potential to transform traditional project management practices. Key areas of learning include the use of AI-enabled tools for project scheduling, resource optimisation, cost estimation, progress tracking, predictive analytics, risk identification, and timely decision-making. Emphasis will also be placed on understanding how data-driven insights and intelligent automation can help project managers anticipate potential delays, improve resource utilisation, strengthen coordination among stakeholders, and enhance overall project performance. The programme also provides an opportunity to discuss practical challenges associated with adopting AI in complex projects, including data quality, technology integration, organisational readiness, and responsible use of AI. By bringing together professionals from the power generation, transmission, infrastructure, energy, and allied sectors, the programme encourages the exchange of industry experiences and best practices. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
