/P 164 0 R
/E (During the session, Dr. Kumar discussed the significance and applications of near-infrared \(NIR\) photodetectors, highlighting their growing importance in areas such as energy efficiency, energy security, defence, and national security. He explained the two-step epitaxial growth of germanium \(Ge\) on silicon \(Si\) substrates and discussed key aspects of device performance, providing participants with insights into the challenges and opportunities associated with advanced semiconductor devices.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (Dr. Kumar also briefly discussed flexible solar cells and their potential for niche applications, particularly their integration into building-integrated photovoltaic \(BIPV\) systems, where flexible and lightweight solar technologies can offer advantages in applications with architectural and structural constraints.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (The session was attended by more than 100 participants from across India, including students, researchers, faculty members, and professionals. The expert session provided valuable insights into emerging materials and device technologies at the intersection of semiconductors, optoelectronics, energy efficiency, and renewable energy.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
